# --- Model provider -------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Database: ONE CONNECTION PER ROLE (R13-conn) ---------------------------
# Decided 8 September 2026: one LOGIN role per worker role, and therefore one
# POOL per role rather than one connection that assumes roles. A pool cannot
# become another role, so a SQL injection reached through the retrieval path
# cannot write a §4.0.7 safety event — reasoner_role holds no grant on
# safety.red_flag_event and no way to acquire one.
#
# ALL THREE ARE REQUIRED. Since R10g there is no fallback: src/lib/db.ts
# refuses to construct a pool with no connection string of its own. Falling
# back would run retrieval as hp_app and fail with a permission error three
# frames inside a PL/pgSQL function, which reads as a broken grant rather than
# a missing secret.
#
# hp_app is the role that takes untrusted user input. HP-RB-001 §2: the
# application must never connect as owner or superuser. It holds SELECT on no
# health attribute and INSERT on no safety row — verified, not assumed.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://hp_app:...@127.0.0.1:5432/healthplus
# The profile read and the knowledge lookup. The only application role holding
# EXECUTE on principal.fetch_attribute_envelope (migration 040) and the
# evidence retrieval path (migrations 042/043).
DATABASE_URL_REASONER=postgres://reasoner_role:...@127.0.0.1:5432/healthplus
# The red-flag scan and its safety-event writes.
DATABASE_URL_REDFLAG=postgres://redflag_role:...@127.0.0.1:5432/healthplus

# No migration sets any of these passwords: ALTER ROLE ... PASSWORD is
# CLUSTER-WIDE, so a migration setting one would change that credential on
# every database in the cluster — and a password in a migration is a password
# in git. Set them out of band; ../DEPLOY.md §2 says how.

# --- Region / residency (HP-ADR-003, HP-ADR-004) ---------------------------
# All rows written by this service are pinned to this region. Never derive it
# from request IP or Accept-Language — it is a property of the DEPLOYMENT, not
# of a request, and it travels in the connection startup packet so there is no
# window in which a connection exists without one.
DATA_REGION=IN

# --- Per-subject key (ADR-003 §2.4) ----------------------------------------
# EXACTLY 32 bytes, base64-encoded. subjectKey.ts refuses anything else rather
# than deriving quietly.
#
# This REPLACED SUBJECT_HMAC_KEY, and the replacement is the point. The old
# variable was a single process-wide HMAC secret standing in for the
# per-subject subject_key table, and under it ERASURE DELETED NOTHING: every
# pseudonym stayed recomputable from a user_id and one env var. This key wraps
# a per-subject DEK the database mints, so principal.erase_subject nulling the
# salt makes the link from an audit row back to a person unrecoverable by
# anyone, including us — which is what lets HP-LB-001's audit-vs-erasure
# reconciliation leave obs.response_audit standing.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32     # or: head -c 32 /dev/urandom | base64
#
# Rotating it means re-wrapping every subject DEK, not replacing a string.
SUBJECT_KEY_WRAPPING_KEY=base64:...

# --- Auth (HP-SEC-001) ------------------------------------------------------
# HS256 shared secret used to verify Supabase-issued JWTs (src/lib/auth.ts).
# If this project moves to Supabase's asymmetric (ES256) signing keys,
# auth.ts needs a JWKS URL instead — see its header comment.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=...

# --- Prompt / policy versions (HP-ESC §6.3/§6.4) ---------------------------
# The classifier and safety-propose prompts live in src/lib/prompts/registry.ts
# and carry their own versions, so no classifier version is read from here.
#
# RED_FLAG_RULESET_VERSION IS GONE. It used to select the active row-set in
# safety.red_flag_rule. R3 replaced it with
# safety.adopted_rule_set(jurisdiction, language), because an env var can name
# a rule set that was never clinically adopted and a function that filters on
# `clinically_adopted` cannot. Setting it now does nothing.
#
# POLICY_VERSION is written into every obs.response_audit row; it defaults to
# 'unspecified' rather than failing, so an unset value is visible in the audit
# trail rather than silent.
PROMPT_VERSION_COMPOSE=compose-2026.08.1
POLICY_VERSION=HP-SCHEMA-001-v0.4

# --- Side-effect dispatcher -------------------------------------------------
# Optional, and inert until something listens on it. There is no durable queue
# behind this ping any more: the review obligation is recorded in
# obs.response_audit.review_state before the dispatcher runs, and every skipped
# dispatch logs at ERROR. See src/lib/pipeline/sideEffectDispatcher.ts.
SIDE_EFFECT_DISPATCH_URL=http://localhost:4001/internal/dispatch

# --- Seeding (development and CI only) -------------------------------------
# scripts/seed-real.ts runs on its OWNER connection, never db(), because hp_app
# holds INSERT on nothing it writes — principal, safety and evidence — and must
# keep holding none. There is deliberately no fallback to DATABASE_URL.
SEED_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:...@127.0.0.1:5432/healthplus
